{"objective":"Close the gaps between what EKA knows and what an agent can discover and safely act on, without changing the underlying model.","scope":"1. Generate a machine-readable description of the whole command surface from the command definitions, including mutation risk, flag types, repeatability, and output schema identifiers; extend `--json` and add a bound to every list command. 2. Give `discard` a confirmation gate matching `transition`, and advertise destructiveness in machine-readable annotations. 3. Add an additive validity horizon to the knowledge envelope plus a staleness query surface, so freshness is expressible without breaking existing corpora. Exit criterion: an agent learns any command's contract in one call, an unconfirmed discard deletes nothing, and staleness is answerable for an artifact and for a domain.","outOfScope":"Not in this wave: migrating the MCP protocol version, adding prompts or resource subscriptions, and any change to how refusals are shaped. Those are recorded decisions or separate concerns. Freshness is scoped to expressibility plus one query surface, not to automated re-verification of knowledge against code."}